1|0@Edmonton^1440198550#cub8ejn:Sickify$:I will agree this is a problem. I think part of it is the price of cabs though. I would prefer to go out and have a drink or two and not worry about driving, because I've taken a cab. Last time I did this, to a pub that is 5 minutes away, it cost me $25 each way, plus a tip. That's ridiculous. So instead I drive, have two beer and wait a few hours, while everyone else continues to drink, which is not ideal. I am being responsible, but it would be so easy to be irresponsible, and very likely not get caught. Uber could very well be a very good thing for lowering the number of impaired drivers. And honestly, the penalties should not be the deterrent, the possibility of killing someone should be the deterrent. You drink and drive and get a huge fine, okay, you can live with that and move forward with your life. You drink and drive, and kill little Jimmy who lives 2 houses down, you will be haunted for the rest of your life.
