-3|0@Edmonton^1440262876#cubxliw:Sirpedroalejandro$:I've driven hammered about a dozen times over the last 10 years, only once did I go through a check stop WITH an open bottle in my car, for a moment I thought of turning into the fields and driving off but I said fuck it and went through and they just waved me through. I can drive fine if I wasn't blackout drunk, the times I was I would actually push my seat back, park somewhere and take a nap. Otherwise you learn what side roads to take to avoid the police. I've seen dozens of cars get pulled over for driving reckless on the weekends, 90% of the time in trucks. Nothing will change it until cars can self drive and drunks have no control. Fact remains that getting home in a city like Edmonton with no metro or public transport past a certain hour is tough without a car. Any of you ever tried taking a cab on the weekend? You're going to wait hours and then the bill for a 20 minute ride is going to be like $40. I find driving while tired/sleepy is far more dangerous, I've done the close your eyes for a second on an empty highway only to realize you closed them for like 5 seconds. Give people actual options and they'll probably use them.
